Materials structure and observation — Cambridge DoITPoMS (@mat-doitpoms-structure: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_57315283EDNWKYC1PQE23G2AKF
University of Cambridge, Department of Materials Science and Metallurgy, DoITPoMS teaching and learning packages. [Collection](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/index.php).

Read complete named packages with their questions: [Atomic Scale Structure](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/atomic-scale-structure/index.php), [Crystallography](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/crystallography3/index.php), [Miller Indices](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/miller_indices/index.php), [Tensors](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/tensors/index.php), [Texture](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/crystallographic_texture/index.php), [Dislocations](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/dislocations/index.php), [Solid Solutions](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/solid-solutions/index.php), [Polymer Basics](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/polymerbasics/index.php), [Glass Transition](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/glass-transition/index.php), [Microstructural Examination](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/microstructural_exam/index.php), [Optical Microscopy](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/optical-microscopy/index.php), [Diffraction](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/diffraction/index.php) and [X-ray Diffraction](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/xray-diffraction-2/index.php). Follow [Slip](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/slip/index.php) and [Fibre Composites](https://www.doitpoms.ac.uk/tlplib/fibre_composites/index.php) when indicated.

Direct retrieval on 30 October 2026 succeeded after web-preview HTTP 403 responses. Package indexes and selected packing, polycrystal, polymer morphology, dislocation, microscopy, diffraction and tensor pages were inspected. Live simulations, films and every linked page were not all exercised. The inspected footer states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 except where otherwise noted; retain each package's contributor and third-party credits. These are selected readings, not an imported collection. All media remain external.

